  "verdict": "Overall TP-rate=0.893 (n=34154). Logistic: contexts significantly shifting TP-rate vs (nonLOH x neutral) = C(loh_status, Treatment(reference='nonLOH'))[T.LOH]; C(cn_class, Treatment(reference='neutral'))[T.gain]; C(cn_class, Treatment(reference='neutral'))[T.loss]; C(loh_status, Treatment(reference='nonLOH'))[T.LOH]:C(cn_class, Treatment(reference='neutral'))[T.gain]; n_cpg. LOH main effect lowers TP-rate (OR=0.36, p=5.3e-20). Higher coverage raises TP-rate (OR/CpG=1.004, p=6.6e-10). Within LOH, cnLOH is MORE FP-enriched than abnormal-CN (OR=0.89, p=0.0093). ",
  "caveats": [
    "Single sample (HCC1395) -> no cross-sample generalization.",
    "FP small: 3,643 FP positions genome-wide; loss-CN cells especially sparse (LOH.loss n=239, nonLOH.loss n=173) -> Fisher/exact used, underpowered cells flagged.",
    "cn_class is tumor median_cn (gain dominates, n=26,029); 'neutral'=CN2. Within LOH, neutral==cnLOH (1:1); on nonLOH side neutral=ordinary diploid.",
    "TP-rate here is ClairS-TO precision proxy on the ASM-eligible position set (positions with >=1 paired-CpG axis), NOT genome-wide caller precision.",
    "is_tp definition: SEQC2 HighConf sSNV truth membership (TP=30,511 analyzed; FP=4,842 caller FP of which 3,643 land on ASM-eligible positions)."
  ]
}